---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const upworkUrl = 'https://www.upwork.com/services/product/writing-translation-professional-sops-and-clear-process-documentation-2098097452881572813?ref=project_share';
---
<BaseLayout title="Selected Project Work" current="" description="Selected short-term project services from Richard J. Allen, including SOP development, workflow documentation, training and onboarding guides, support procedures, and documentation cleanup.">
<section class="project-hero"><div class="container project-hero-grid">
  <div>
    <div class="project-badge">SECONDARY PROJECT-WORK PATHWAY</div>
    <div class="eyebrow light">Selected Project Work</div>
    <h1>Clear documentation for work that matters.</h1>
    <p>My primary focus is finding the right long-term operations or customer-success leadership role. I also take on selected, well-defined short-term projects when a team needs an important process documented, organized, or made easier to use.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button button-light" href="mailto:rjallencareer@gmail.com?subject=Project%20work%20inquiry">Discuss a project</a><a class="project-hero-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href={upworkUrl}>View Upwork SOP service →</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="doc-workflow" aria-label="Documentation workflow from source material through structure, review, and usable delivery">
    <div class="workflow-title">DOCUMENTATION WORKFLOW</div>
    <div class="workflow-stack">
      <div><span>01</span><strong>Source</strong><small>notes · screenshots · forms · interviews</small></div>
      <i>↓</i>
      <div><span>02</span><strong>Structure</strong><small>steps · handoffs · decisions · ownership</small></div>
      <i>↓</i>
      <div><span>03</span><strong>Review</strong><small>clarity · completeness · consistency</small></div>
      <i>↓</i>
      <div><span>04</span><strong>Deliver</strong><small>usable SOP · guide · workflow · standard</small></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="project-proof-band"><div class="container project-proof-grid" aria-label="Selected documentation experience">
  <div><strong>125+</strong><span>SOPs encompassed by a year-long modernization program</span></div>
  <div><strong>25+</strong><span>legacy procedures inventoried and updated</span></div>
  <div><strong>~10</strong><span>functional groups coordinated in the OED effort</span></div>
  <div><strong>Dozens</strong><span>of historical HawkSoft sales policies and procedures documented</span></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Focused services</div><h2>Small, practical scopes built around proven experience.</h2></div><p class="section-note">I keep project work close to areas I have actually done in operations, support, training, customer experience, and process improvement.</p></div>
  <div class="grid two value-grid project-service-grid">
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">SOP</div><h3>SOP creation & standardization</h3><p>Turn notes, screenshots, forms, interviews, and existing materials into clear Standard Operating Procedures with consistent structure and ownership.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">FLOW</div><h3>Process & workflow documentation</h3><p>Document who does what, when, with which inputs, systems, handoffs, decisions, and escalation points.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">LEARN</div><h3>Training & onboarding guides</h3><p>Create practical instructions and reference material that help employees or customers learn a process and repeat it consistently.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">OPS</div><h3>Support-operations procedures</h3><p>Document customer-support, troubleshooting, escalation, service, handoff, quality, and related operating procedures.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">FIX</div><h3>Existing-document cleanup</h3><p>Review older procedures for unclear language, inconsistent structure, duplicated material, gaps, missing ownership, and difficult-to-follow steps.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">GOV</div><h3>Documentation governance</h3><p>Help organize standards, repositories, review practices, and maintenance guidelines so documentation stays useful after the initial project ends.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section project-fit-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Why this is a natural fit</div><h2>Project services grounded in actual operating work.</h2></div><p class="section-note">Documentation is strongest when it understands the work around the document.</p></div>
  <div class="project-fit-grid">
    <article><span>PROCESS</span><strong>Year-long SOP program leadership</strong><p>Led an Oregon Employment Department modernization and governance program across roughly 10 functional groups, ultimately encompassing 125+ SOPs.</p></article>
    <article><span>OPERATIONS</span><strong>Procedures across sales and support</strong><p>Historical HawkSoft records show creation, updating, and documentation of dozens of sales policies and procedures in addition to support, training, and operating documentation.</p></article>
    <article><span>PRODUCT</span><strong>Product & training documentation</strong><p>At The Kotter Group, documented Bridge XLerator features and benefits, usage instructions, user stories and business cases; also created customer education, release/procedure documentation, webinars, and training content.</p></article>
    <article><span>CONTEXT</span><strong>Operations perspective</strong><p>Documentation work is informed by experience managing people, workflows, reporting, quality, change, customer operations, warehouse/supply operations, and cross-functional execution.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section upwork-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="upwork-panel">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Upwork Project Catalog</div>
      <h2>Professional SOPs & clear process documentation</h2>
      <p>My Upwork freelancer profile and SOP-focused Project Catalog service were approved and published in September 2026. Upwork provides a convenient way to purchase a defined documentation project; direct project inquiries are also welcome.</p>
      <p class="small">No freelance client ratings, earnings, or completed-project outcomes are presented here yet because this is a new project-work channel.</p>
    </div>
    <aside><div class="project-start-label">TWO WAYS TO START</div><a class="button" href="mailto:rjallencareer@gmail.com?subject=Project%20work%20inquiry">Email about a project</a><a class="button secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href={upworkUrl}>View Upwork service</a></aside>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section tight"><div class="container"><div class="fulltime-banner"><strong>Full-time opportunities remain my primary focus.</strong><span>Project work is a complementary option for organizations that need a defined piece of operational documentation or enablement work completed now.</span><a href="/contact/">Contact me about a role or project →</a></div></div></section>

<style>
  .project-hero{padding:4.6rem 0 4rem;color:#fff;background:radial-gradient(circle at 84% 18%,rgba(183,121,31,.22),transparent 24%),linear-gradient(128deg,#102f55 0%,#153e75 58%,#5c4b2d 120%)}.project-hero-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.08fr) minmax(380px,.92fr);gap:3rem;align-items:center}.project-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.8rem,6vw,5rem);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:.55rem 0 1.1rem}.project-hero p{font-size:1.12rem;color:#e4ebf3;max-width:720px}.project-badge{display:inline-flex;padding:.28rem .55rem;margin-bottom:.8rem;border-radius:999px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.1);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18);font-size:.66rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#f1e3bd}.project-hero-link{color:#fff;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;align-self:center}.doc-workflow{padding:1.2rem;border-radius:24px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.07);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18);box-shadow:0 24px 55px rgba(0,0,0,.16)}.workflow-title{font-size:.7rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.14em;color:#ead9a8;margin:.1rem 0 .9rem}.workflow-stack{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.workflow-stack>div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:44px 1fr;grid-template-rows:auto auto;column-gap:.7rem;padding:.75rem .85rem;border-radius:14px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.12)}.workflow-stack>div span{grid-row:1/3;align-self:center;width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:50%;display:grid;place-items:center;background:rgba(255,255,255,.1);font-size:.68rem;font-weight:900;color:#f0e0b9}.workflow-stack strong{font-size:1rem}.workflow-stack small{color:#d6e0e8}.workflow-stack>i{font-style:normal;text-align:center;line-height:1;color:#d2b974;font-weight:900}.project-proof-band{background:#fff;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.project-proof-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr)}.project-proof-grid>div{padding:1.25rem;border-right:1px solid var(--border)}.project-proof-grid>div:last-child{border-right:0}.project-proof-grid strong{display:block;font-size:1.7rem;line-height:1;color:var(--gold)}.project-proof-grid span{display:block;margin-top:.4rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.84rem;line-height:1.35}.project-service-grid .card{transition:transform .18s ease,box-shadow .18s ease}.project-service-grid .card:hover{transform:translateY(-2px);box-shadow:0 14px 32px rgba(23,32,42,.07)}.project-fit-section{background:linear-gradient(180deg,#f8fafc,#fff)}.project-fit-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:1rem}.project-fit-grid article{padding:1.25rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;background:#fff;box-shadow:0 10px 28px rgba(23,32,42,.05)}.project-fit-grid span{font-size:.68rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.11em;color:var(--accent-2)}.project-fit-grid strong{display:block;margin:.4rem 0;font-size:1.08rem}.project-fit-grid p{margin:0;color:var(--muted)}.upwork-section{background:linear-gradient(180deg,#f5f8fc,#f7f8fa)}.upwork-panel{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.5fr) minmax(270px,.5fr);gap:1.2rem;padding:1.5rem;border-radius:22px;background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--border);box-shadow:0 16px 40px rgba(23,32,42,.06)}.upwork-panel h2{margin:.25rem 0 .7rem}.upwork-panel>div p{max-width:760px}.upwork-panel aside{padding:1.1rem;border-radius:16px;background:linear-gradient(180deg,#f8fbff,#f5faf9);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.7rem;justify-content:center}.upwork-panel aside .button{text-align:center}.project-start-label{font-size:.68rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--accent)}.fulltime-banner{padding:1.25rem 1.4rem;border-radius:18px;background:var(--blue-soft);border-left:5px solid var(--accent);display:grid;gap:.35rem}.fulltime-banner span{color:var(--muted)}.fulltime-banner a{font-weight:800}
  @media(max-width:950px){.project-hero-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.doc-workflow{max-width:700px}.project-proof-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.upwork-panel{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  @media(max-width:700px){.project-fit-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.project-proof-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.project-proof-grid>div{border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.project-proof-grid>div:last-child{border-bottom:0}}
  @media(max-width:600px){.project-hero{padding:3.4rem 0}.workflow-stack>div{grid-template-columns:40px 1fr}}
  @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.project-service-grid .card{transition:none}.project-service-grid .card:hover{transform:none}}
</style>
</BaseLayout>
